IO-53: list the worst link or node even when it is the first one

report_writeMaxFlowTurns() and report_writeNonconvergedStats() printed
"All links are stable." / "Convergence obtained at all time steps." when
the top entry of their ranking had index <= 0. An empty ranking has index
-1 (stats_findMaxStats); index 0 is the first link or node of the model.
Test for index < 0, as report_writeMaxStats() already does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-53_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/report.c b/src/legacy/engine/report.c
index 604507d..70f7d8d 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/report.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/report.c
@@ -991,7 +991,7 @@ void report_writeMaxFlowTurns(TMaxStats flowTurns[], int nMaxStats)
     WRITE("********************************");
     WRITE("Highest Flow Instability Indexes");
     WRITE("********************************");
-    if ( nMaxStats <= 0 || flowTurns[0].index <= 0 )
+    if ( nMaxStats <= 0 || flowTurns[0].index < 0 )
         fprintf(Frpt.file, "\n  All links are stable.");
     else
     {
@@ -1016,7 +1016,7 @@ void report_writeNonconvergedStats(TMaxStats maxNonconverged[], int nMaxStats)
     WRITE("*********************************");
     WRITE("Most Frequent Nonconverging Nodes");
     WRITE("*********************************");
-    if (nMaxStats <= 0 || maxNonconverged[0].index <= 0 ||
+    if (nMaxStats <= 0 || maxNonconverged[0].index < 0 ||
         maxNonconverged[0].value < 0.00005)
         fprintf(Frpt.file, "\n  Convergence obtained at all time steps.");
     else
